2. Create web_app/lib/presentation/screens/connections/connections_screen.dart with the full implementation described in detail below.

--- DATA MODELS (top of file, private) ---
class _ConnectionItem { final String id; final String requesterId; final String receiverId; final String status; final String createdAt; }
class _UserProfile { final String id; final String fullName; final String? academicLevel; final String? role; final int reputationPoints; }

Parse _ConnectionItem from Map<String,dynamic>: id, requesterId, receiverId, status, createdAt.
Parse _UserProfile from Map<String,dynamic>: id, fullName (from 'fullName'), academicLevel, role, reputationPoints (default 0).
_UserProfile.initials: split fullName by space, take first char of up to 2 words, uppercase.

--- PROVIDERS ---
All providers are FutureProvider.autoDispose placed at file scope.

a) connectionsProvider — GET /connections. Returns List<_ConnectionItem>.
   final connectionsProvider = FutureProvider.autoDispose<List<_ConnectionItem>>((ref) async { ... });
   Parse resp.data['data'] as List → cast to List<Map<String,dynamic>> → map to _ConnectionItem.

b) pendingReceivedProvider — GET /connections/pending/received. Returns List<_ConnectionItem>.

c) pendingSentProvider — GET /connections/pending/sent. Returns List<_ConnectionItem>.

d) userProfileCacheProvider — FutureProvider.autoDispose.family<_UserProfile?, String> with userId as param.
   GET /users/:id/profile. Returns _UserProfile? (null on error, never throws).
   Wrap in try/catch: on error return _UserProfile(id: userId, fullName: 'Unknown Student', ...).

e) _findStudentsProvider — FutureProvider.autoDispose.family<List<_UserProfile>, String> with query as param.
   IMPORTANT: The backend /search endpoint only searches courses/resources/questions — it does NOT search users.
   Strategy: This provider must call GET /users/:id/profile for individual lookups. However, since there is no
   user-list or user-search backend endpoint accessible to students, the Find Students tab will show a
   search-by-matric-or-name UI that is honest about the limitation:
   - If query is empty or < 2 chars, return [].
   - Otherwise call GET /users/search?q=<query> (optimistic — if backend adds it later the provider
     will automatically work; if 404, catch and fall back).
   - Practical implementation: load accepted connections and filter their partner profiles
     by name match against the query (case-insensitive substring). Return all unique matches.
   NOTE TO IMPLEMENTER: The 'Find Students' tab must show a clear in-UI notice:
   'Student search is limited. You can find students you are already connected with, or try entering
    an exact name. A dedicated student search feature is coming soon.' Display this above the search field.

--- SCREEN CLASS ---
class ConnectionsScreen extends ConsumerStatefulWidget { const ConnectionsScreen({super.key}); }

State class _ConnectionsScreenState extends ConsumerState<ConnectionsScreen> with SingleTickerProviderStateMixin {
  late TabController _tabController;
  final _searchCtrl = TextEditingController();
  String _searchQuery = '';
  // Per-item loading state: keyed by connectionId (for accept/remove/cancel buttons)
  final Map<String, bool> _actionLoading = {};

  @override initState() { super.initState(); _tabController = TabController(length: 3, vsync: this); }
  @override dispose() { _tabController.dispose(); _searchCtrl.dispose(); super.dispose(); }

  // Action helpers — all show SnackBar on success/failure, invalidate providers on success
  Future<void> _sendRequest(String receiverId) async { ... }
  Future<void> _acceptRequest(String connectionId) async { ... }
  Future<void> _removeConnection(String connectionId) async { ... }
  Future<void> _cancelRequest(String connectionId) async { ... }
  // Each action: set _actionLoading[key] = true, call api, on success invalidate relevant providers,
  // on error show SnackBar with AppColors.error background.

  @override Widget build(BuildContext context, WidgetRef ref) {
    returns Scaffold with:
      backgroundColor: AppColors.background,
      appBar: AppBar(
        title: const Text('Connections'),
        backgroundColor: AppColors.navyDark,
        foregroundColor: Colors.white,
        elevation: 0,
        bottom: TabBar(
          controller: _tabController,
          labelColor: AppColors.cyanBright,
          unselectedLabelColor: AppColors.textOnDarkSub,
          indicatorColor: AppColors.cyanBright,
          labelStyle: const TextStyle(fontFamily: 'Nunito', fontWeight: FontWeight.w700, fontSize: 13),
          tabs: [
            const Tab(text: 'My Connections'),
            Tab(text: 'Requests', icon: _RequestsBadge()),  // shows badge count if pending received > 0
            const Tab(text: 'Find Students'),
          ],
        ),
      ),
      body: TabBarView(
        controller: _tabController,
        children: [
          _MyConnectionsTab(actionLoading: _actionLoading, onRemove: _removeConnection),
          _RequestsTab(actionLoading: _actionLoading, onAccept: _acceptRequest, onReject: _removeConnection, onCancel: _cancelRequest),
          _FindStudentsTab(searchCtrl: _searchCtrl, searchQuery: _searchQuery, onQueryChanged: (q) => setState(() => _searchQuery = q), onSendRequest: _sendRequest, actionLoading: _actionLoading),
        ],
      ),
  }
}

--- TAB WIDGETS ---

_MyConnectionsTab: ConsumerWidget, watches connectionsProvider.
  .when(
    loading: () => _ConnectionSkeleton(),  // 5 skeleton cards
    error: (e,_) => _ErrorWidget(message: 'Could not load connections.', onRetry: () => ref.invalidate(connectionsProvider)),
    data: (connections) {
      if (connections.isEmpty) return _EmptyState(icon: Icons.people_outline, message: 'No connections yet. Find students to connect!');
      return ListView.separated(padding: Responsive.getPaddingEdgeInsets(context), itemCount: connections.length, separatorBuilder: (_,__) => const SizedBox(height: 8),
        itemBuilder: (ctx, i) {
          final conn = connections[i];
          final currentUserId = ref.watch(currentUserProvider)!.id;
          final peerId = conn.requesterId == currentUserId ? conn.receiverId : conn.requesterId;
          return _ConnectionCard(connectionId: conn.id, peerId: peerId, actionLoading: actionLoading,
            action: 'remove', onAction: () => onRemove(conn.id));
        });
    },
  )

_RequestsTab: ConsumerWidget, watches both pendingReceivedProvider and pendingSentProvider.
  Shows two sections in a SingleChildScrollView:
  Section header 'Received Requests' + received list (each card has Accept + Reject buttons)
  Section header 'Sent Requests' + sent list (each card has Cancel button)
  Loading/error/empty handled per section.

_FindStudentsTab: ConsumerStatefulWidget (or just stateless receiving state from parent).
  Shows the limitation notice (info banner: Icon(Icons.info_outline) + text, background AppColors.info.withValues(alpha:0.1)).
  TextField for search (AppColors.surfaceAlt fill, prefixIcon: Icons.search).
  Watches _findStudentsProvider(_searchQuery).
  Results shown as cards with Send Request button (disabled if already connected — but for simplicity,
  show the button and let the API return a 409 which is caught and shown as a SnackBar).
  If query < 2 chars: show prompt text 'Enter a name to search for students.'.
  Empty result: _EmptyState(icon: Icons.search_off_outlined, message: 'No students found for that name.').

--- SHARED CARD WIDGET ---
_ConnectionCard: ConsumerWidget.
  Accepts: connectionId, peerId, actionLoading map, action label(s), callback(s).
  Internally watches userProfileCacheProvider(peerId).when(
    loading: () => _SkeletonListTile(),
    error: (_,__) => ListTile(title: Text('Unknown Student')),
    data: (profile) => ListTile with leading CircleAvatar(initials), title fullName, subtitle role+level,
      trailing action button(s).
  )
  CircleAvatar: radius 22, backgroundColor AppColors.primary.withValues(alpha:0.15),
    child Text(profile?.initials ?? '?', style TextStyle color AppColors.primary fontWeight w700).
  Action buttons: OutlinedButton or ElevatedButton; show CircularProgressIndicator(strokeWidth:2) when _actionLoading[connectionId] == true.
  Remove button: foregroundColor AppColors.error, side BorderSide(color: AppColors.error).
  Accept button: backgroundColor AppColors.success.

--- SKELETON WIDGETS ---
_SkeletonListTile: ListTile with placeholder containers for all fields (Container with color AppColors.surfaceAlt).
_ConnectionSkeleton: ListView of 5 Card(_SkeletonListTile()) items.

--- EMPTY / ERROR WIDGETS ---
_EmptyState: Center column with Icon(64), SizedBox(16), Text(hint style AppColors.textHint).
_ErrorWidget: Center column with Icon(Icons.error_outline, AppColors.error, 48), Text, ElevatedButton('Retry').

--- REQUESTS BADGE ---
_RequestsBadge: ConsumerWidget that watches pendingReceivedProvider and shows a red dot badge if count > 0.
  Use Stack + Positioned for the badge dot (Container 8x8 red circle).
  Only show inside the Tab icon area — use Tab(child: Row(...)) pattern.

